![Foto de Battlecreek Coffee Roasters en Unsplash](cover.jpg)

The official documentation says:

- use [_Phoenix.Component_](https://hexdocs.pm/phoenix_live_view/Phoenix.Component.html) to compartmentalize/reuse markup
- use [_Phoenix.LiveComponent_](https://hexdocs.pm/phoenix_live_view/Phoenix.Component.html) to compartmentalize state, markup, and events
- use nested [_Phoenix.LiveView_](https://hexdocs.pm/phoenix_live_view/Phoenix.LiveView.html) to compartmentalize state, markup, events, and error isolation

## Some Context

- `handle_params`: A function triggered in the parent LiveView with the url params.

- `mount`: A function triggered in the parent LiveView and LiveComponents for setting the initial values.

- `update`: A function triggered in the parent LiveView and LiveComponents for updating the assigns in a component instance.

- `preload`: A function triggered in the parent LiveView and LiveComponents for updating the assigns in multiple instances of the component.

- `handle_event`: A function triggered by the HTML/JS side.

- `handle_info`: A function triggered by using `send(self(), args)` inside a `live_component`. Handled by the parent liveview.

- `pipeline`: A function that is called when defining the live_view or live_component.

- `@myself`: A target to specify in LiveViews or LiveComponents. `phx-target={@myself}`

**lib/my_web/my_web.ex**

```elixir
def live_view do
    quote do
      use Phoenix.LiveView,
        layout: {MyWeb.Layouts, :app}

      unquote(html_helpers())
    end
end
```

Used as

```elixir
defmodule MyWeb.Live.Home do
  use MyWeb, :live_view
```

This is how I understand the main differences

## LiveView

- Creates a **socket**
- Handlers: `handle_event`, `handle_info`, `handle_params`, `mount`, `update`, `preload`.
- Can use `@myself` to handle events (requires id)
- Renders html

[live_render/3](https://hexdocs.pm/phoenix_live_view/Phoenix.LiveView.Controller.html#live_render/3)

## LiveComponent

- Uses the **socket** defined in the Parent _LiveView_
- Handlers: `handle_event`, `mount`, `update`, `preload`.
- Can use `@myself` to handle events (requires id)
- Renders html

```elixir
<.live_component module={MyModule} id="unique_id" {assigns} />
```

## Component

- Only renders html

```elixir
<MyComponent.render {assigns} />
```

## Comparison

``` =html
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Item</th><th>LiveView</th><th>LiveComponent</th><th>Component</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>renders html</td><td>✅</td><td>✅</td><td>✅</td></tr>
    <tr><td>can use <code>@myself</code> (requires id)</td><td>✅</td><td>✅</td><td>❌</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>mount</code></td><td>✅</td><td>✅</td><td>❌</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>update</code></td><td>✅</td><td>✅</td><td>❌</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>preload</code></td><td>✅</td><td>✅</td><td>❌</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>handle_event</code></td><td>✅</td><td>✅</td><td>❌</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>handle_info</code></td><td>✅</td><td>❌</td><td>❌</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>handle_params</code></td><td>✅</td><td>❌</td><td>❌</td></tr>
    <tr><td>creates a socket</td><td>✅</td><td>❌</td><td>❌</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
```
